# Specification Section 24 requires LF line terminators in every text artifact the tool
# produces, and Appendix C requires LF in every conformance fixture. Normalizing in the
# working tree as well as in the index keeps fixtures byte-exact on Windows checkouts.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.nupkg binary
*.snupkg binary

# Conformance fixtures are compared byte-for-byte and must never be transformed.
conformance/** -text
tests/**/fixtures/** -text

# Spike corpora are evidence, not source. Normalization silently emptied the CRLF fixture in
# spikes/yaml-comments of every CR byte, which voided the line-ending dimension of a verdict
# that KNOWN-LIMITS.md cites. Evidence that the toolchain rewrites is not evidence.
spikes/** -text